---
//! The tunnel and the way to a host: one post-quantum WireGuard tunnel for
//! everything, pairing by PIN (This computer → Devices, from the app's demo:
//! scripts/capture-hero.sh), and NAT traversal without a relay, the path
//! docs/networking.md describes.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Card from './Card.astro';
import Point from './Point.astro';
import Section from './Section.astro';
import { TUNNEL } from '../lib/facts';
import devices from '../assets/windows/devices.webp';
---

<Section
  id="private"
  lead="Private, from anywhere."
  rest="One post-quantum tunnel, no ports to forward."
>
  <Card slot="cards" title="Post-quantum, end to end">
    Picture, sound, input and the clipboard share one WireGuard tunnel with ML-KEM-768, at {TUNNEL.encrypt1200} per
    1,200-byte packet. A device pairs once, with a PIN.
    <div slot="visual" class="bleed">
      <div class="shot">
        <Image
          src={devices}
          alt="Helio's Devices page on a Mac: MacBook Air asks to pair, with a field for its PIN, above three paired devices, each with what it may do."
          widths={[640, 960, 1280]}
          sizes="(max-width: 860px) 90vw, 640px"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </Card>
  <Card slot="cards" title="No ports to forward">
    Hosts publish sealed records on the BitTorrent DHT, and both sides punch through their routers, with no relay and
    no VPN.
    <div slot="visual" class="pad">
      <svg class="path" viewBox="0 0 420 150" role="img" aria-labelledby="path-title">
        <title id="path-title">
          Your computer and the host each behind a router, finding each other through the DHT and connecting directly.
        </title>
        <g class="dashed">
          <path d="M70 96 Q 70 29 160 29"></path>
          <path d="M350 96 Q 350 29 260 29"></path>
        </g>
        <path class="direct" d="M120 118 H 300"></path>
        <g class="node">
          <rect x="20" y="96" width="100" height="44" rx="10"></rect>
          <text x="70" y="123">Your Mac</text>
        </g>
        <g class="node">
          <rect x="300" y="96" width="100" height="44" rx="10"></rect>
          <text x="350" y="123">gaming-pc</text>
        </g>
        <g class="cloud">
          <rect x="160" y="12" width="100" height="34" rx="17"></rect>
          <text x="210" y="34">DHT</text>
        </g>
      </svg>
    </div>
  </Card>
  <Point slot="points" icon="key" title="Permissions for each device">
    Choose what each device may do: watch, type, click, copy and paste, start apps.
  </Point>
  <Point slot="points" icon="copy" title="The clipboard, both ways">
    Text, images, files and folders; on macOS and Windows, never a password manager’s copies.
  </Point>
  <Point slot="points" icon="globe" title="One exception">
    When both sides are behind symmetric NAT, nothing relays the stream: forward UDP 47800 to the host.
  </Point>
</Section>

<style>
  /* The window runs off the card's bottom and right edges. */
  .bleed {
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 0;
    padding-left: 28px;
    margin-bottom: -1px;
  }

  .bleed .shot {
    border-right: 0;
    border-bottom: 0;
    border-radius: 12px 0 0 0;
  }

  .pad {
    padding: 0 28px 28px;
  }

  .path {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .path text {
    fill: var(--text);
    font-family: var(--font);
    font-size: 13px;
    text-anchor: middle;
  }

  .node rect {
    fill: var(--card-2);
    stroke: var(--line-2);
  }

  .cloud rect {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--sky-5);
    stroke-dasharray: 3 4;
  }

  .cloud text {
    fill: var(--text-2);
  }

  .dashed path {
    fill: none;
    stroke: rgb(var(--sky-5-rgb) / 0.5);
    stroke-dasharray: 3 5;
  }

  .direct {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--sky-2);
    stroke-width: 2;
  }
</style>
